# Project Technology Stack (Stack Rules)

> **This file belongs to the `Stack` layer** and is customized for your project during `/l1-onboard`. Running `npx l1dder sync` preserves your changes to this file.

---

## 1. Tech Stack Matrix

| Layer | Selection (Configured during `/l1-onboard`) | Purpose & Key Constraints |
|-------|---------------------------------------------|---------------------------|
| **Language & Runtime** | `[e.g., TypeScript 5.x (Node 22) / Python 3.12 / Go 1.24]` | Strict typing, compile-time / CI typechecking. |
| **Frontend / UI** | `[e.g., React 19 + Tailwind CSS v4 + Vite / Next.js / —]` | Component UI isolated from core domain logic. |
| **Backend / Core** | `[e.g., Fastify / Hono / FastAPI / Go stdlib / —]` | Deep domain modules (`Deep Modules`) with clean public seams. |
| **Data & Validation** | `[e.g., PostgreSQL + Drizzle / SQLite / Zod / Pydantic]` | Schema validation at trust boundaries (`Fail fast`). |
| **Package Manager** | `[e.g., pnpm / uv / go mod / cargo]` | Single lockfile committed to the repository. |
| **Quality & Testing** | `[e.g., ESLint + Prettier + Vitest + Playwright / Ruff + Pytest]` | Seam unit tests and E2E user scenario tests. |

---

## 2. Layer Architecture

```
src/
├── app/                # Entry point, configuration, routing
├── core/               # Domain & business logic (Deep Modules with public Seams)
├── ui/ (or api/)       # Presentation (UI components / HTTP handlers / CLI commands)
├── data/ (or store/)   # Persistence, schema validation, external integrations
└── shared/             # Shared types, constants, utilities
tests/                  # Integration and E2E tests
```

---

## 3. Project Makefile & `Edit → Sanitize → Verify` Loop

```makefile
make dev            # start local dev environment
make build          # build production artifact
make lint           # run linter
make format         # auto-format code
make typecheck      # run type checker
make test           # run unit / integration tests
make test-e2e       # run E2E tests (if applicable)
make ci             # lint + typecheck + test + build
```
